INSERT INTO `hallofmemorytbl` VALUES (3,6,'Cutler','Laura','momobitpicture.png','LauraPeanutWinningAvatar.png','Laura C Cutler <br> 1927 - 2020','Peanuts <br> 6 year Member','Summers would find Laura collecting heart shaped rocks and blue sea glass on singing beach and later on Marthas Vineyard. Laura loved to laugh and she lived and enjoyed life in a way that made others lives fuller. Laura was an Overseer Ameriti of the Boston Museum of Science. She loved nature which resulted in her support of the Massachusetts Audubon Society.','Laura joined us in our first year. She was our first Daredevil Ducks Champion! She was always a competitive and enthusiastic member. She loved football, especially Joe Namath!'),(9,14,'Bruehl','Anthony (Tony)','TonyBruehlHallofMemory.png','RemingtonHallofFamePicture1.png','Robert Anthony (Tony) Bruehl <br> 1943 - 2026','Tanya Gorman, Tony Bruehl and Remington <br> 10 year Member','Tony served as an employee of the State of Georgia for 32 years from 1986 - 2008. Tony was loved, and will be remembered, for his kindness, generosity, dry wit, love of golf, and Mountain Cove - his beloved cabin in the North Georgia mountains.  He died with his \'best fur-buddy\' Nixon providing love and warmth across his chest.','Tony and Tanya with their dog Remington, joined the Daredevil Ducks in 2015! In 2019 they won the coveted Daredevil Ducks Trophy! We were lucky enough to have met Tony. During a tour of their home, Tony showed us a painting painted and given to Tony by Commander Cody! If you don\'t understand that - then you are too young! We will miss Tony very much. '),(4,23,'Jamieson','Judson','JudsonJamiesonHallofMemoryPicture.png','JudsonJamiesonHallofMemoryAvatar.png','Judson B Jamieson <br> 1935 - 2020','18 Wheeler <br> 5 year Member','Judson was a loving & devoted husband, father, grandfather & great grandfather. He was an old time Maine-iac from Camden, ME. He started his career as a truck driver, moving families all over the U.S., which he loved.  After graduating from Los Angeles Univ, he worked as Head of Respiratory Therapy at New England Memorial Hospital. Jud also served our country in the Army at Fort Eustis in VA.','Judson  (Jud) joined us in our second year. He was also a competitive and enthusiastic member. Jud came within one win of the Daredevil Ducks trophy in 2016, loosing to his grand daughter in the final game!'),(6,30,'Brady','Dan','DanBradyHallofMemoryPicture.png','SummervilleAvatarHallFame.png','Dan Brady <br> 1954 - 2024','Sville 5<br> 8 year Member','Dan was a proud former Marine, and a talented photographer and musician. He was also a gifted craftsman who could build just about anything out of wood. Dan always rooted for the underdog, but when pressed did claim the Eagles as his team as he was born and raised in Wilmington, Delaware. He is remembered as a loving Husband, Father, Grandpa and a great dog dad!','Dan and his wife Marilyn joined us way back in 2015. They were always competitive and in the hunt! All that culminated in the winning of our coveted Daredevil Ducks Trophy in 2023!'),(7,31,'Allard','Kay','AuntieKay.png','KayAvatarHallofMemory.png','Kay Allard <br> 1925 - 2024','Red Bird <br> 8 year Member','Known as Auntie Kay, she always had a smile on her face and a positive outlook on life. Kay thoroughly enjoyed playing tennis and golf. Kay and her husband Herb, spent their married life cultivating beautiful flowers and vegetable gardens. After Herb passed away in 2012, she immersed herself in her extended family. She will be missed by many.','Auntie Kay joined us in 2015. She was a tenacious competitor who leaned heavily on the Boston Globe sports pundits! When she would lose, she would blame them for their bad advice! She never won the big one, but she always loved the game.'),(1,35,'Therrien','Steve','SteveTherrienHallofMemoryPicture.png','SteveTherrienHallofMemoryAvatar.png','Steven A. Therrien <br> 1950 - 2018','Fighting Duck <br> 2 year Member','Steve was a loving and caring husband and Father with wife Sandy, daughter, son and 3 grandchildren.  He had a successful career in software technology in both programming and sales. Steve was a member of several clubs, such as Haverhill Kiwanis, Cedardale Tennis, Old Newbury Golf and Newburyport Racquet Club. ','Steve joined in our second year along with his wife Sandy (SandyT).  He had a great run and is missed from our members.'),(8,36,'Therrien','Sandy','SandyTherrienHallofMemoryPicture.png','SandyTherrienHallofMemoryAvatar.png','Sandy J. Murphy - Therrien <br> 1951 - 2024','SandyT  <br> 7 year Member','Sandy was a loving and caring wife and Mother with a daughter, son, 3 grandchildren and a great grandchild.  Sandy was a fun and loving person who enjoyed almost every sport.  She was especially talented playing tennis, pickleball and roller skating.  Sandy always enjoyed having fun, and being with her family and friends.','Sandy joined us in 2016 and has been an active player since. She and her husband Steve joined together, and got her two grandsons Jeffery and Patrick to join, with one of them winning in 2022.   Sandy was always a competitive and enthusiastic member.'),(2,50,'Putnam','Nancy','nancy-putnam.png','NancyPutnamHallofMemoryAvatar.png','Nancy Putnam <br> 1931 - 2020','Snow Storm <br> 3 year Member','Nancy was devoted to her husband George, and her standard poodles. She and her late husband greatly enjoyed their saltwater farm on Mount Desert Island, Maine. She served on the boards of several nonprofit institutions in Maine, including Island Readers & Writers, Woodlawn Museum, Land & Garden Preserve and the Island Institute.','Nancy joined us in our third year. She and her husband George invited us with our Airstream down east to their humble Maine home. It was there that we sold her on becoming a member.'),(5,65,'Kretlow','Fred','FredKretlowHallofMemoryPicture.png','FredKretlowHallofMemoryAvatar.png','Fredrick P Kretlow <br> 1941 - 2021','Captain Coconut <br> 4 year Member','Fred was a great Husband and Father. He was born in Whitefish Bay, WI. He was a valued bank auditor for Palmer Bank and later became a Vice President, CDM for SunTrust. Fred was an avid mariner and Siesta Key sunset chaser.  He will be missed dearly, but knowing he is safe in heaven.','Fred joined us in our fourth year. We had the pleasure of meeting him and his wife in Florida at Turtle Bay. We sat on the beach and watched the sun set. It is always our pleasure to meet one of our members, and so it was with Fred and his wife Linda. ');

