SandyKennedy1.png','member','SandyLRudman@gmail.com',0,'','Portland','ME','',1,'207-379-3762',0,0,0,'','1','SandyR',NULL,'active','2022-11-09 17:40:46',NULL),(78,'Pete Prisco',1,'Pete Prisco','Male',1,'CBSSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Ft Lauderdale','FL','',1,'',0,0,1,'CBSSports.coms senior NFL columnist brings more than 30 years of football reporting experience to the job and his famed Priscos Picks to the Westgate Super Contest. A mainstay in the CBS Expert Picks section, Pete is a former radio host and beat writer for the Jacksonville Jaguars.','1','Pete Prisco',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:42:31',NULL),(79,'Patrick Trana',1,'PatrickT','Male',1,'PatrickTranaAvatar.png','member','',0,'','','WA','',1,'425-337-8820',0,0,1,'','1','PatrickT',NULL,'inactive','2025-02-24 13:07:58',NULL),(80,'Phil Simms',1,'Phil Simms','Male',1,'CBSSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Franklin Lakes','NJ','',1,'',0,0,1,'Born Nov 3, 1954 in Springfield, Kentucky.  He attended St. Dominics Elementary, then joined Southern High School.  Enrolled at Morehead State University, after graduation he was signed with the New York Giants in 1979.  During his entire career, 1979 to 93, he played 164 games and completed 2,576 passes with 199 touchdowns and 157 interceptions.  He won Super Bowl XXI and XXV, and was Most Valuable Player in Super Bowl XXI.  Currently, he works as a Sportscaster for CBS network, and was featured in several movies and TV shows.','1','Phil Simms',NULL,'inactive','2019-10-06 18:58:40',NULL),(81,'Kurt Warner',1,'Kurt Warner','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Scottsdale','AZ','',1,'',0,0,1,'Born June 22, 1971, in Burlington, Iowa.  He attended Regis High School, and then attended the University of Northern Iowa.   He was invited to train with the Green Bay Packers, but was cut just a few weeks later.  He spent years doing average minimum wage jobs before playing for the Iowa Barnstormers in 1995-97.  In 1998, he signed a contract with the St Louis Rams as a free agent for over a year before replacing Trent Green as the Rams quarterback.  As the QB he scored over 36 touchdowns and passed for over 4,000 yards. He even helped this team to win the Super Bowl XXXIV.  In 2002 he go to Super Bowl XXXVI, and faced the Patriots, but lost 17 to Patriots 20.  2004 he played as a New York Giant. 2005 he played with the Arizona Cardinals and reached the Super Bowl XLIII in 2009.  Sadly he lost 27 to 23 to Pittsburg.  Announcing his retirement in 2010.  He joined the NFL Network in 2010. He would work on several football shows; NFL Total Access, Thursday Night Football, and Monday Night Football.','1','Kurt Warner',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:36:42',NULL),(82,'Boomer Esiason',1,'Boomer Esiason','Male',1,'CBSSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','','','',1,'',0,0,1,'','1','Boomer Esiason',NULL,'inactive','2019-09-25 05:18:14',NULL),(83,'NFL Fan Picks',1,'NFL Fan Picks','Other',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Culver City','CA','',1,'',0,0,1,'NFL pundits, analysts and their media networks tracking every one of the talking heads weekly NFL picks, and the team performance of all pundits from their network company. And the NFL network free picks, FOX NFL picks, ESPN NFL picks and all weekly NFL pundits picks from NFL network.','1','NFL Fan Picks',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:38:06',NULL),(84,'Bill Cowher',1,'Bill Cowher','Male',1,'CBSSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','','','',1,'',0,0,1,'','1','Bill Cowher',NULL,'inactive','2019-09-25 05:16:11',NULL),(85,'Steve Mariucci',1,'Steve Mariucci','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Monte Sereno','CA','',1,'',0,0,1,'Nicknamed Mooch, he was born Nov 4, 1955 in Iron Mountain, Michigan.  At Northern Michigan University (NMU) in Marquette he was a 3 time All-America Wildcats Quarterback.  Mariucci signed with the Hamilton Tiger-Cats of the Canadian Football League in May 1978, but was released a month later.  He began his coaching career at Northern Michigan University 1978 to 79, then to Cal State Fullerton 1980 to 82 and onto Louisville 1983 to 84. His first pro position was as a receivers coach for the USFL\'s Orlando Renegades in 1985.  He joined the USC staff in 1986, then moved to the coaching staff at the Univ of California, Berkeley in 1987.  In 1990 to 91, he with the Golden Bears.  He moved to the NFL, and became the QB coach for the Green Bay Packers in 1992 under head coach Mike Holmgren.  After 4 years with the Packers, he returned to Cal as head coach in 1996.  In 1997 he went to the 49ers and compiled a .583 record, and earned playoff berths 4 times.  In 2003 he was head coach of the Detroit Lions until 2005.  Mariucci coached a high 8 players inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame in Canton, Ohio. He is now an American sportscaster for the NFL Network on NFL GameDay, NFL GameDay Morning, as well NFL GameDay Highlights.','1','Steve Mariucci',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:43:26',NULL),(86,'Michael Irvin',1,'Michael Irvin','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Plano','TX','',1,'',0,0,1,'Nicknamed The Playmaker he was born March 5, 1966, in Ft Lauderdale, FL as the 15th of 17 siblings.  He became a football star at St. Thomas Aquinas High School.  He was heavily recruited by the University of Miami, the Miami Hurricanes, under coach Jimmy Johnson.  He set school records for career receptions, receiving yards and touchdown receptions.  He was on the team that defeated the Oklahoma Sooners 20 to 14 in the 1988 Orange Bowl national championship game.  The Dallas Cowboys drafted him in the 1st round in 1988.  From 1988 to 1999 the Cowboys with Irving made 4 straight NFC Championship Games and captured 3 Super Bowl titles, Super Bowl XXVII and Super Bowl XXVIII, and the Super Bowl XXX.  He retired from football in 2000 he was forced into early retirement due to a non life threatening cervical spinal cord injury during a game.  August 4, 2007, Irvin was inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame.  Now an ESPN and NFL sports analyst and commentator.','1','Michael Irvin',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:58:16',NULL),(87,'Marshall Faulk',1,'Marshall Faulk','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','','','',1,'',0,0,1,'','1','Marshall Faulk',NULL,'inactive','2018-09-03 00:49:00',NULL),(88,'Rich Eisen',1,'Rich Eisen','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','',NULL,'',1,'',0,0,1,'','1','Rich Eisen',NULL,'inactive','2017-09-24 16:11:41',NULL),(89,'Las Vegas Insider',1,'Las Vegas Insider','Other',1,'LasVegasInsider.png','expert','',0,'','Fort Lauderdale','FL','',1,'',0,0,0,'The Global Leader In Sports Gaming Information.  The best collection of handicapping talent in the world.  Provide a world of gaming analysis, stats and up to the second odds and news.  Constantly create the best presentation of stats and analysis for every type of sports gaming enthusiast.','1','Las Vegas Insider',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:37:40',NULL),(90,'Frank Schornagle',1,'Goalie29','Male',1,'FrankSchornagle.png','member','frank@biltmorefamilyoffice.com',0,'','Orlando','FL','',1,'407-353-6197',0,6,0,'','1','biltmore',NULL,'active','2022-11-30 12:26:27',NULL),(91,'TeamRankings.com',1,'TeamRankings.com','Other',1,'TeamRankings.png','expert','TeamRankings.com',0,'','','CA','',1,'',0,0,1,'Launched from Stanford Univ dorm room in 2000, TeamRankings is from a math geek passion project into the web #1 source for algorithmic sports predictions and data. Currently publish over 200,000 pages of projections, stats, rankings, and odds.  Thousands of sports bettors and office pool players use our premium services to get an edge, and our data is referenced by the country top sports media outlets.','1','TeamRankings.com',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:39:12',NULL),(92,'Toby McCormack',1,'Kookier','Female',1,'TobyMcCormackAvatar10222018.png','member','',0,'','Gloucester','MA','',1,'(978) 853-6214',0,0,1,'','1','Kookier',NULL,'inactive','2025-02-24 13:02:46',NULL),(93,'Craig Donnelly',1,'Day Walker','Male',1,'CraigDonnellyAvatarB.png','member','CDonnell351@gmail.com',0,'','Ft. Wayne','IN','',1,'260-415-4482',0,0,0,'','1','Day Walker',NULL,'active','2022-11-30 14:35:06',NULL),(94,'Pam Peck',1,'Profit Center','Female',1,'Pam Peck Avatar 1 A.png','member','',0,'','','MA','',1,'???(508) 740-1361???',0,0,1,'','1','Profit Center',NULL,'inactive','2025-02-24 13:08:55',NULL),(95,'Ron Jaworski',1,'Jaws (Ron Jaworski)','Male',1,'NFLNetworkSportsAnalyst.png','expert','',0,'','Voorhees Township','NJ','',1,'',0,0,0,'Nicknamed Jaws or The Polish Rifle, he was born March 23, 1951, in Lackawanna, NY. After high school, he turned down a professional baseball offer from the St Louis Cardinals to attend college at Youngstown State University as a QB for the Penguins, earning a selection in the Senior Bowl.  He was drafted and played 4 years for the LA Rams from 1973 to76.  From 1977 to86 he played for the Philadelphia Eagles, starting 116 consecutive games.  In 1980, he led the Eagles in their 1st Super Bowl, but lost Super Bowl XV to the Oakland Raiders, 27 to10.  He was named the MVP of the NFL in 1980.  1987 to88 he signed with the Miami Dolphins for 2 years, then he signed with the Kansas City Chiefs for 1989.  In 1990 he retired from football.  In 1988, he joined the WIP AM as a sports commentator and hosted the Ron Jaworski Show.  In 1990, he joined ESPN and worked as a game analyst, game site reporter, sideline reporter, and studio analyst. Here is Ron announcing the top 5 quarterbacks in 2014 NFL draft. He is now part owner of the Philadelphia Soul of the Arena Football League, and serves as Chairman for the AFL.  He is also a primary investor in the Elite Football League of India.  He is the owner of Ron Jaworski Golf Management that oversees several clubs in New Jersey.','1','Jaws',NULL,'inactive','2019-06-06 17:57:13',NULL),(96,'Gery Delgado',1,'Gzzer1','Male',1,'GeryDelgadoAvatar.png','member','',0,'','Murrieta','CA',